    "result_text": "All 70 tests pass with BUILD SUCCESS across two consecutive runs (the single earlier BUILD FAILURE was transient \u2014 no error was reported and it did not reproduce).\n\n## Summary\n\nI released version 2 of the owner identity. Changes:\n\n**OpenAPI spec (`openapi.yml`)** \u2014 the DTO source (generated at build time):\n- Added a new `OwnerIdentity` schema grouping `memberId`, `identityKey`, `householdId`.\n- On `Owner`: removed those three top-level properties, added `identity: $ref OwnerIdentity` and a top-level integer `apiVersion`.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** (read/response projection):\n- Added `apiVersion` = `2` and an `identity` object (built from the owner's stored `memberId`, `householdId`, and the rederived `identityKey`); removed the top-level `identityKey` mapping.\n- Rederived `identityKey` to the **V2** algorithm \u2014 SHA-256 over `\"V2|\" + telephone + \"|\" + email + \"|\" + soundex`.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** (creation + dedup + audit):\n- `identityKey` rederived to the identical **V2** input, so duplicate detection still matches the read side.\n- `computeHouseholdId` now hashes `\"V2|\" + normalizedLastName + \"|\" + postcode` (still a pure function of last name + postcode, so households still share it \u2014 Cp11).\n- `memberId` now embeds a **V2 region code** via a new `regionCodeV2` helper (plain region + `\"V2\"`, e.g. `NSWV2261A2B3C4D7`).\n- Audit `OWNER_CREATED` event moved to schema version 2 with an added `schemaVersion: 2`, carrying the V2 `memberId`.\n\n**Preserved (V2 tag never leaks into user-facing fields):**\n- `locality` stays the plain region (`NSW`), `timezone` unchanged, and `ownerSegment`'s derived region stays plain \u2014 so a Sydney owner still resolves `NSW` / `Australia/Sydney` / `STANDARD_METRO`.\n\nBecause the fixed `V2` tag is mixed in with a delimiter that can't appear in any V1 input (region prefixes are followed by digits under V1, never `V2`), every V2 identifier is disjoint from its V1 counterpart. Request fields are unchanged.",
