    "probe_text": "Verified against source. Here is the complete ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners`, handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (the HTTP binding and `@Valid @RequestBody` come from the generated `OwnersApi` interface; the body binds to the DTO `OwnerFieldsDto`, not the `Owner` entity).\n\n## Before the method body runs\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Missing role \u2192 403.\n2. **Bean Validation on the DTO** (`@Valid`), on `OwnerFieldsDto`:\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words, ` '-` separators)\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (same, optional trailing `.`)\n   - `title`: `@Size(max 10)`\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email`: `@Size(3..255)`, `@Email`\n   - `address` / `addressLine1` / `addressLine2`: `@Size(max 255)`\n   - `postcode`, `sharesHousehold`: no constraints\n   - Any failure \u2192 `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 400. No nested-object validation (pets are not part of the create body).\n\n## Inside the method body (exact order)\n\n3. **Idempotency replay** \u2014 reads the `Idempotency-Key` header; if that key was seen before, re-fetches the original owner (`findOwnerById`) and returns it with **200 OK**, short-circuiting everything below.\n4. **`rejectMissingOrBlankFields`** \u2014 null/blank `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `telephone`, or address (in either flat or structured form) \u2192 `RequiredFieldsMissingException` \u2192 400.\n5. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity** (`ownerMapper.toOwner`); `id` and `pets` ignored. *(side-effect: object construction)*\n6. **`applyAddress`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 prefers structured `addressLine1/2`, normalizes (upper-cases, collapses whitespace, expands `ST`/`RD`/`AVE`, etc.), and composes the flat `address` field.\n7. **`normalizeTelephone`** *(validation + side-effect)* \u2014 coerces to E.164; invalid \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` \u2192 400. Stored back on the owner.\n8. **`normalizeEmail`** *(validation + side-effect)* \u2014 if present: syntactic check (`InvalidEmailException` \u2192 400), lower-cases it, then rejects disposable domains (`DisposableEmailDomainException` \u2192 400). Stored back on the owner.\n9. **`validatePostcode`** \u2014 if present: must be 4 digits and within the region range for the city, else `InvalidPostcodeException` \u2192 400.\n10. **`rejectFutureRegistrationDate`** \u2014 a supplied date after today \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` \u2192 400.\n11. **Default registration date** *(side-effect)* \u2014 if null, set to `LocalDate.now()`.\n12. **`rollToBusinessDay`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 rolls the registration date forward past weekends and fixed 2026 public holidays.\n13. **`rejectDailyLimitReached`** \u2014 \u2265100 owners already registered on that date \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` \u2192 **429**.\n14. **`rejectCityAtCapacity`** \u2014 \u226550 owners in that city (case-insensitive) \u2192 `CityOwnerLimitExceededException` \u2192 **409**.\n15. **`computeHouseholdId`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 SHA-256 of `V2|normalizedLastName|postcode`, first 12 hex chars.\n16. Read `sharesHousehold` flag from the DTO.\n17. **`rejectDuplicateIdentity`** \u2014 exact identity-key match against non-deleted owners \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` \u2192 **409**.\n18. **`assignPossibleDuplicate`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 soft duplicate detection by last-name soundex + exact postcode (skipped if `sharesHousehold` or no postcode); sets `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf`.\n19. **`generateMemberId`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 `<REGIONV2><FY><HASH8><Luhn check>`, de-duplicated with a `-n` suffix (reads all owners' member IDs).\n20. **Derived fields set** *(side-effects)* \u2014 `namesakeCount` (`countNamesakes`), `householdSize` (`countHouseholdSize`), `membershipLevel` (`computeMembershipLevel`), `bulkSignupWarning` (`isBulkSignupDay`, >80/day), `capacityWarning` (`isCityApproachingCapacity`, 40\u201349). Each re-reads all owners.\n21. **`clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 `@Transactional` persist via `ownerRepository.save`. **Entity-level Bean Validation runs here at flush**: `firstName`/`lastName`/`address`/`city` `@NotEmpty`, and `telephone` `@Pattern(^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$)`.\n22. **Record idempotency key** *(side-effect)* \u2014 maps the key to the new owner's id.\n23. **Map entity \u2192 `OwnerDto`** for the response (derives displayName, initials, salutation, fiscal year, membership points/level, locality, timezone, segment, risk flag, self link, etc.).\n24. **`AUDIT.info(...)`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 human-readable audit log line.\n25. **`emitOwnerCreatedEvent`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 writes a schema-v2 JSON line to the `AUDIT` logger with a process-wide sequence number. *(Not a Spring `ApplicationEvent` \u2014 just a log emission.)*\n26. **`enqueueWelcomeNotification`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 writes a line to the `NOTIFY` logger. *(Also just logging, not a real queue.)*\n27. **Set `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header** and return **201 CREATED** with the DTO.\n\n## Notes worth flagging\n\n- **All the domain validation and side-effects live in the controller, not the service.** `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner` is a thin `@Transactional` wrapper around `ownerRepository.save`; there is no password encoding, email sending, or event publishing in the service.\n- **No JPA lifecycle callbacks, no `@EntityListeners`, no JPA auditing, and no Spring event listeners** exist anywhere in this flow. The only `ConstraintValidator` in the codebase (`PetAgeValidator`) applies to pets and does not fire here.\n- **Transaction boundaries are split:** the many pre-save `findAllOwners` reads (steps 13\u201320) each run in their own read-only transaction, separate from the single write transaction in step 21 \u2014 so the capacity/duplicate/limit checks are not atomic with the save."
